`fleece` is **absolutely worth mining**, but I would not make it the new base repo. It is a donor of several unusually good primitives that fit the Letta + Hydra + `cg` direction almost perfectly.

The funny part is that `fleece` already contains an earlier, trading-specific version of what we just rediscovered as the Moltwork Lab.

## What `fleece` already got right

Its core structure is:

```text
fixed strategies
     ↓
pools
     ↓
evolvable allocation genome
     ↓
"school"
     ↓
league
     ↓
rank / prune / breed
     ↓
graveyard
     ↓
Hydra remembers everything
     ↓
Orca reads history
     ↓
proposes next experiments
```

That is explicitly how the repo describes itself.

The **really valuable bits** are not the options logic. They are the general mechanisms underneath it.

### 1. The graveyard

This is excellent and should go straight into Moltwork.

Fleece never deletes bad schools. Bottom performers become tombstones and remain evidence for future learning. The league then mines previous failures rather than repeatedly rediscovering them.

For Moltwork:

```text
WorkerMutation
     │
     ├─ promoted
     │
     └─ rejected
            │
            ▼
        GRAVEYARD
            │
       why rejected
       tasks failed
       metrics regressed
       cost regression
       parent version
```

Then when Letta proposes:

> “Maybe I should start doing X.”

Moltwork can answer:

> We tried effectively-X three generations ago. It improved presentation but reduced factuality 11%.

That is exactly the kind of organizational memory a Lab should develop.

