# 6. The experimental discipline should definitely survive

Fleece is much more rigorous than most “self-improving agent” projects.

It has:

* hash-locked scenarios
* immutable control systems
* held-out evaluation
* preregistered experiments
* evidence grades
* bootstrap/Wilson statistical evaluation
* explicit invalidation
* append-only findings

Its findings ledger even records when adaptive approaches **lose** rather than pretending every experiment succeeded.

That's exactly the attitude Moltwork needs.

The Lab should say:

```text
Hypothesis:
Three candidate submissions improve quality.

Test:
80 historical jobs.

Result:
+1.7% quality
+71% compute

Verdict:
REJECT
```

instead of:

> The agent reflected and became smarter!

This is probably one of your strongest differentiators.

