# 9. Canonical files → derived Hydra graph: KEEP THIS

Fleece explicitly treats Hydra as derived, rebuildable memory rather than canonical truth. Its experiment records remain local/canonical and Hydra is reconstructed from them.

That is exactly right.

Our new architecture should be:

```text
CANONICAL

RunEvent
Trajectory
Artifact
Evaluation
Outcome
MemoryCommit
WorkerVersion

immutable/event-sourced

      │
      ├────► Hydra
      │       graph projection
      │
      ├────► analytics
      │
      ├────► cg
      │
      └────► receipts/proofs
```

Never:

```text
Hydra is the only place the experience exists
```

because databases change.

